  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieved 0.650 acc / 0.628 F1, a large jump over its singleprofile counterpart config_004 (0.520/0.498), confirming that multiprofile aggregation is the dominant design lever so far. scvi_n200 also outperformed pca_n2000 in singleprofile (0.520 vs 0.485). Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether the aggregation mechanism matters—i.e., whether a transformer aggregator can capture inter-profile dependencies beyond simple averaging. This experiment (config_006) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding the best-performing encoder (scvi_n200) and multiprofile setting fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_005. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it exploits the strongest evidence (multiprofile + scvi_n200) while resolving a critical design choice (aggregation type) that will directly inform which aggregation to pair with multimodal fusion in later experiments, without introducing additional confounds."
}

